//
// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING:
// Norway is a CONFIDENT, PERMISSIVE market (Denmark-tier) — and the
// sharpest possible contrast with Sweden next door. Norway has
// opplaeringsplikt (a duty of EDUCATION), not compulsory attendance.
// Under the new Education Act (opplaeringslova, adopted 9 June 2023,
// in force 1 August 2024), privat grunnskoleopplaering i hjemmet is
// one of three lawful ways to fulfil the duty (§ 22-5):
// - NO prior approval or application — written NOTIFICATION to the
//   child's local school / municipality in good time before starting
//   (child's name, fodselsnummer, address, start date, parents'
//   contact details);
// - NO formal pedagogical qualification required of parents (stated
//   explicitly by e.g. Bergen kommune);
// - content must be equivalent to public grunnskole education;
// - the municipality has a statutory RIGHT AND DUTY of supervision
//   (tilsyn): under the new Act the first tilsyn must happen within
//   THREE MONTHS of starting, and common practice is two per school
//   year; municipal practice varies — some (e.g. Baerum) expect a
//   learning plan before the school year and an annual report;
// - if tilsyn cannot be conducted properly or the education is found
//   inadequate, the municipality decides the child must attend
//   school. Cooperation with tilsyn is therefore non-negotiable and
//   our pages say so plainly;
// - parents bear the costs; no textbook loans or compensation; the
//   individual-assessment (grades) rules do not apply, so there is no
//   ordinary vitnemal — videregaende admission happens on individual
//   assessment, and every young person retains the statutory right to
//   videregaende (§ 5-1).
// POST-16: videregaende is a RIGHT, not a duty — voluntary. Norway
// therefore has Sweden's clean post-16 A-Level window ON TOP OF an
// open notification-based framework before 16. Use both.
// Smartious's role: parents hold responsibility for the home
// education; Smartious delivers the live curriculum, teaching, and
// the documentation (plans, progress records, assessment) that
// municipal tilsyn draws on. Never imply Smartious replaces the
// parents' legal responsibility.
// Norway is EEA, not EU. Currency NOK. University admission via
// Samordna opptak with foreign qualifications assessed against the
// GSU requirements; IB and A-Levels are established routes.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

